          "Stage 5: Synthesis of Proposed Inventory Audit Adjustments (SUD Schedule): The simulator aggregates all identified inventory misstatements: $1.8M in physical count shrinkage, $3.4M in improperly capitalized manufacturing variances, and $6.8M in NRV impairment write-downs. It evaluates cumulative inventory misstatements ($12.0M) against planning materiality ($18M) and performance materiality ($12.6M), generating the formal Proposed Audit Journal Entries (PAJEs) to adjust the balance sheet before issuing the audit report.",
          "Audit Committee Governance Reporting and Management Discussion: In accordance with PCAOB AS 1301, the simulator compiles the complete inventory assurance docket for presentation to the Board Audit Committee. The reporting package articulates the key findings from physical count observations, presents the standard cost variance allocation models, highlights the empirical evidence supporting NRV write-downs, and reviews management's planned improvements to warehouse perpetual tracking systems.",
          "Engineering Specialist Collaboration and Physical Valuation Audits: In specialized aerospace environments involving complex work-in-process (such as multi-stage satellite payloads and advanced avionics flight computers), the financial auditor collaborates directly with independent engineering valuation specialists under PCAOB AS 1210 / ISA 620. The simulator models the auditor's review of the specialist's credentials, underlying physical inspection methodology, stage-of-completion assessments, and scrap valuation models, ensuring that complex technical WIP assets are evaluated with rigorous professional competence.",
          "It compiles physical count observation memos, dock cut-off manifests, perpetual roll-forward schedules, standard costing BOM recalculations, and NRV market price comparisons, providing strong evidential support that substantiates the existence, completeness, and valuation of inventory. The inventory simulator automates physical count testing, roll-forwards, variance allocations, and NRV models into a rigorous audit pipeline.",
          "By replacing fragmented manual spreadsheets with a unified, code-driven substantive inventory audit engine, statutory assurance firms uncover concealed physical losses, prevent improper cost capitalization, and protect capital markets from inventory overstatement."
