          "Corporate Governance and Audit Committee Presentation: In accordance with PCAOB AS 1301 and ISA 260, the simulator prepares the final subsequent events briefing for the Board Audit Committee. The briefing explains the economic rationale behind booking the $15.0M Type 1 bankruptcy write-down and provides the technical disclosures for the $32.0M Type 2 warehouse casualty loss, ensuring full governance transparency.",
          "Audit Working Paper Documentation and PCAOB Inspection Readiness: Finally, the simulator indexes all analytical review memoranda, board minute extracts, bankruptcy filings, fire casualty loss assessments, and dual-dating legal memos directly into electronic Lead Schedule SE-1 under PCAOB AS 1215. This comprehensive documentation provides strong proof of thorough completion fieldwork, withstanding regulatory inspection from the PCAOB and national audit oversight bodies. Every analytical ratio calculation, subsequent cash verification trace, and disclosure footnote is cross-referenced with standardized electronic audit tickmarks.",
          "Engagement Team Wrap-Up and Management Sign-Off Protocol: In addition, the engine coordinates the final administrative wrap-up protocol. It archives the completed analytical review checklists, logs partner sign-offs on all Lead Schedules, and verifies that the Chief Financial Officer and General Counsel have reviewed and accepted the dual-dated report disclosures prior to the release of the SEC Form 10-K filing.",
