    "description": "Master the rigorous audit of an entity's ability to continue as a going concern under ISA 570 (Revised), PCAOB AS 2415, and FASB ASC Subtopic 205-40. Learn to evaluate the statutory look-forward assessment window (one year after financial statement issuance under US GAAP vs at least 12 months from balance sheet date under IFRS), identify negative financial trends and operational warning indicators, evaluate the feasibility and probability of management's mitigating plans, perform liquidity cash burn stress testing and debt covenant headroom analysis, structure appropriate going concern footnote disclosures, formulate the 'Material Uncertainty Related to Going Concern' explanatory paragraph, and deploy automated going concern survival simulators.",
